      "text": "Starting Wednesday, April 1, 2026, Japan Airlines (JL) will operate at the Ninoy Aquino International Airport (NAIA) Terminal 3 from NAIA Terminal 1.\n\nOther international airlines that operate at NAIA Terminal 3 were:\n\nAir China (CA)\n\nAll Nippon Airways (NH)\n\nCathay Pacific (CX)\n\nCebu Pacific (5J)\n\nChina Eastern (MU)\n\nChina Southern Airlines (CZ)\n\nEmirates (EK)\n\nEthiopian Airlines (ET)\n\nEtihad Airways (EY)\n\nGreater Bay Airline (HB)\n\nGulf Air (GF)\n\nHong Kong Express (UO)\n\nJeju Air (7C)\n\nJetstar Japan (JQ)\n\nKLM Royal Dutch Airlines (KL)\n\nQantas (QF)\n\nQatar Airways (QR)\n\nThai Airways (TG)\n\nTurkish Airlines (TK)\n\nRoyal Brunei Airlines (BI)\n\nScoot (TR)\n\nShenzhen Airline (ZH)\n\nVietnam Airlines (VN)\n\nSingapore Airlines (SQ)\n\nAir France (AF)\n\nUnited Airlines (UA)\n\nAir Canada (AC).\n\nInternational airlines that operate at NAIA Terminal 1 were:\n\nPhilippine Airlines (PR)\n\nAirAsia Philippines (Z2)\n\nAirAsia Berhad (AK)\n\nAir Niugini (PX)\n\nAsiana Airlines (OZ)\n\nChina Airlines (CI)\n\nEva Air (BR)\n\nKorean Air (KE)\n\nKuwait Airways (KU)\n\nMalaysian Air (MH)\n\nOman Air (WY)\n\nSaudia (SV)\n\nXiamen Air (MF)\n\nVietJet Air (VJ)\n\nAir India (AI).\n\nThe airline terminal assignments are part of NAIA’s move to reduce congestion and improve passenger flow and to avoid confusion on which terminal to go.\n\nThe announcements were made by the New NAIA Infrastructure Corporation (NNIC) and the Manila International Airport Authority (MIAA). | via Rudy Santos",
